      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Crossover scenes on Ollama\n\nSame graph as `h3_crossover_batch.json`, but the **H3 LLM Backend** node feeds the Crossover Writer's `llm` socket, so the scenes are written by a local model instead of the Claude Code CLI.\n\n- `model`: pick a discovered `ollama:` / `lmstudio:` / `local:` entry, or *custom* + `model_name` (`ollama:qwen3:14b`, `lmstudio:qwen/qwen3-8b`, `claude:claude-sonnet-5`, `gpt:gpt-5.6` …). Bare Ollama tags like `qwen3:14b` work too.\n- `base_url` for a LAN box (`http://192.168.1.10:11434`), `temperature`, `max_tokens` (multi-scene runs need room).\n- `inline_skill_references`: paste the full H3 reference library into the system prompt (better prompts, needs a big `num_ctx`).\n- Everything else is identical: wardrobe / location locks + one repair turn, template `{vars}`, `session_id` resume (a text-only local session), lists out to the video node, Scenes Join → one video.\n\nUnplug the `llm` socket (or bypass the backend) and the writer is back on Claude Code."
      ],
      "color": "#3d3222",
      "bgcolor": "#1e1c17",
      "title": "APNext — LLM Backend"
    },
